---
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import data from '../data/events.json';
import Subscribe from '../components/Subscribe.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const approxSources = Math.round(data.sourceCount / 10) * 10;
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — Rasa Calendar</title>
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Disclaimer variant="short" />

    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="back"><a href={`${base}/`}>← Back to the calendar</a></p>
        <h1>About</h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="wrap">
      <p class="lede">
        New York City and the metro area around it are full of chances to stay
        close to Indian dance and music, whether you grew up with these forms in
        the diaspora or are meeting them for the first time. There is no single
        place that gathers them all. I kept finding out about events I would
        happily have gone to only after they had happened, because I had no
        reliable way of hearing about them in time.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        Rasa Calendar is my attempt at fixing that for myself and for anyone
        else with the same problem. It is a personal project, put together in
        my spare time.
      </p>

      <h2>What's here</h2>
      <p>
        Indian dance and music across the New York City metro area, covering the
        five boroughs, New Jersey, Long Island and Westchester. That includes
        classical dance forms such as Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Odissi and
        Kuchipudi, Hindustani and Carnatic concerts, semi-classical and fusion
        work, folk, contemporary pieces, and film and popular repertoire. Along
        with performances you will find festivals, talks, workshops and
        community events such as garba nights and Diwali programmes.
      </p>
      <p>
        This calendar is updated weekly with events from ~{approxSources} venue
        calendars. Please treat the venue's own page as the final word on dates,
        prices and tickets.
      </p>

      <h2>Get it by email</h2>
      <p>
        One email a month listing the events added to the calendar since the
        previous one. There is nothing else in it, and every email has an
        unsubscribe link.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is also the way to reach me. Reply to any of those emails, whether
        you have an event to suggest, a correction to a listing, or anything
        else about the calendar.
      </p>
      <Subscribe variant="about" />

      <Disclaimer variant="long" />

      <p class="byline">Created and maintained by Shalaka Kulkarni.</p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap"><p><a href={`${base}/`}>← Back to the calendar</a></p></div>
    </footer>

    <style is:global>
      .masthead {
        background: #15110f; border-bottom: 6px solid var(--turmeric);
        padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) 0 clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      }
      .masthead h1 {
        margin: .4rem 0 0; color: #fff9ec;
        font: 900 clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem)/0.92 var(--font-display);
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -.01em;
        text-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #c4162a;
      }
      .back a, footer a {
        color: var(--turmeric); font: 700 .78rem/1 var(--font-condensed);
        letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      }
      footer a { color: var(--link); }
      .back { margin: 0; }
      main { padding: 2rem 1.25rem 3rem; max-width: 46rem; }
      /* Every paragraph on this page reads at one size, including the opening
         and the disclaimer. Only headings and the small print above them differ. */
      main p, .lede, .disclaimer-long p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; }
      h2 {
        font: 900 1.15rem/1 var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .04em; margin: 2rem 0 .6rem;
        border-left: 10px solid var(--turmeric); padding-left: .7rem;
      }
      .cta-row { margin: .8rem 0 1.2rem; }
      .btn-sub { background: var(--turmeric); color: var(--turmeric-ink); }
      .how { padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }
      .how li { margin-bottom: .7rem; }
      code {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .84rem;
        background: var(--surface-sunk); border: 2px solid var(--rule);
        padding: .1rem .35rem; word-break: break-all;
      }
      footer {
        border-top: 6px solid var(--rule); background: var(--surface-sunk);
        padding: 1.2rem 0 2.5rem;
      }
      .disclaimer-strip {
        margin: 0; background: var(--rail-bg); color: var(--rail-ink);
        text-align: center; padding: .45rem 1rem;
        font: 700 .7rem/1.4 var(--font-condensed);
        letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase;
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--turmeric);
      }
      .disclaimer-long { margin: 2.4rem 0 0; border-top: 3px solid var(--rule-soft); padding-top: 1.2rem; }
      .disclaimer-long h2 {
        font: 900 1.15rem/1 var(--font-display); text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .04em; margin: 0 0 .6rem; border-left: 10px solid var(--turmeric);
        padding-left: .7rem;
      }
      .disclaimer-long p { color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .byline {
        margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.1rem;
        border-top: 3px solid var(--rule-soft); color: var(--ink-muted);
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
